{"provider":"jkw-local","version":1,"sourceType":"DOCX","sourcePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user/65d8ea64-e382-5070-81e6-5dde97f8b555/scratchpad/corpus/fn2/docx/fn2_no_doi_last_then_prose.docx","pdfPath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user/65d8ea64-e382-5070-81e6-5dde97f8b555/scratchpad/corpus/fn2/docx/fn2_no_doi_last_then_prose.pdf","generatedAt":"2026-11-02T06:38:44.062Z","text":"Introduction\nOsteoarthritis is a degenerative joint condition that leads to the gradual breakdown of articular\ncartilage and remodelling of the underlying bone. The patient described morning stiffness\nlasting less than thirty minutes, which is consistent with a mechanical rather than\ninflammatory process (Brophy & Fillingham, 2022).\nManagement should begin with education and a structured exercise programme, because\nstrengthening the quadriceps reduces pain and improves function for most patients. Weight\nreduction is also recommended when the body mass index exceeds the healthy range, and the\nclinician should revisit these goals at every follow-up visit.\nPharmacological treatment is reserved for symptoms that do not respond to conservative\nmeasures. Topical anti-inflammatory agents are preferred before oral agents in older adults,\nsince gastrointestinal and renal risks increase with age and with concurrent medication use.\nScreening recommendations must be reviewed at the same consultation. According to current\nguidance, adults aged forty-five to seventy-five should be offered colorectal cancer screening,\nand women aged forty to seventy-four should be offered biennial mammography unless a\nhigher-risk pathway applies.\nIn summary, the evidence supports a stepped approach that prioritises non-pharmacological\ncare, reserves medication for persistent symptoms, and integrates preventive screening into\nroutine visits so that the patient's long-term health is protected.\nReferences\nOkafor, Chinedu Emmanuel, & Mensah, Abena Serwaa. (2024). The banks that report more are\nthe banks that are trusted more: Evidence from West African lenders and what this means for\nregulators. Journal of Banking Regulation, 25 (3), 301–322. https://doi.org/10.1057/s41261-024-\n00230-1\nNakamura, Hiroshi, Tanaka, Yuki, & Sato, Kenji. (2023). This study shows that disclosure quality\nis higher when boards are independent and when the auditor is one of the large firms. Asian\nReview of Accounting, 31 (4), 512–534. https://doi.org/10.1108/ARA-02-2023-0041\nFernández-García, María José, & López, Juan Carlos. (2022). In emerging markets, green bonds\nare priced differently than conventional bonds because investors value the certification.\nSustainability, 14 (9), 5120. https://doi.org/10.3390/su14095120\nClarityAI. (2025). Sustainable Finance Regulatory Outlook 2025.\nThe findings presented above should be interpreted with care, because the sample covers only\nlisted firms and the observation period ends before the most recent regulatory changes were\nintroduced in the region (Barney, 1991, pp. 99–120).","wordCount":353,"characterCount":2599,"pageCount":1,"auditedItems":58,"pages":[{"pageNumber":1,"start":0,"end":2599,"width":612,"height":792,"rotation":0,"itemCount":58,"items":[{"text":"Introduction","start":0,"end":12,"pageNumber":1,"x":90.1,"y":682.65,"width":72.632,"height":14,"transform":[14,0,0,14,90.1,682.65],"fontName":"g_d7_f1","direction":"ltr","hasEOL":false},{"text":"Osteoarthritis is a degenerative joint condition that leads to the gradual breakdown of articular","start":13,"end":110,"pageNumber":1,"x":90.1,"y":666.45,"width":431.13399999999984,"height":11,"transform":[11,0,0,11,90.1,666.45],"fontName":"g_d7_f2","direction":"ltr","hasEOL":false},{"text":"cartilage and remodelling of the underlying bone. The patient described morning stiffness","start":111,"end":200,"pageNumber":1,"x":90.1,"y":651.95,"width":431.34299999999985,"height":11,"transform":[11,0,0,11,90.1,651.95],"fontName":"g_d7_f2","direction":"ltr","hasEOL":false},{"text":"lasting","start":201,"end":208